# Frontend Portal Conventions

Three portals under `src/pages/`: `voter/`, `officer/`, `admin/`. A page belongs to exactly one portal. Shared UI goes in `src/components/`, never in a portal folder.

## Routing

Each portal sits behind a route guard that checks the authenticated role. The guard controls navigation only.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — treating a hidden control as a permission
{user.role === 'ELECTION_ADMINISTRATOR' && <CloseElectionButton />}
// ...with no role check on the backend route
```

Hiding a control is a usability choice. The backend must reject the call regardless.

## API access

All HTTP goes through typed functions in `src/services/`. Components and hooks never call Axios directly and never build a URL by hand.

```ts
// src/services/remotePolling.ts
export const submitRemotePollingRequest = (input: RemotePollingRequestInput) =>
  api.post<RemotePollingRequest>('/remote-polling/requests', input).then((r) => r.data);
```

## Forms

React Hook Form with a Zod resolver. The Zod schema is the single source of validation truth for a form; do not duplicate rules in JSX.

## Ballots in the UI

Never render or store a voter identifier alongside a candidate choice. Show the ballot's constituency as it came from the API; never compute it from the assigned remote polling centre.

## State

No TanStack Query or Redux. Local state plus the service layer is the agreed scope.
